# Security and Runtime

## Environment and Secrets

- Never hardcode secrets, tokens, API keys, or private identifiers in source files.
- Keep runtime config in environment variables and reference via `process.env`.
- For public browser variables, require `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix.
- Document required env variables when introducing new runtime dependencies.

## Third-Party Scripts and Compliance

- Add analytics/marketing scripts only when gated by project privacy policy.
- Keep consent-dependent behavior in client-only integration components.
- Ensure consent updates are idempotent and do not break page rendering.
- Avoid introducing third-party scripts in route pages; prefer root layout or dedicated integration component.

## Reliability and Safety

- Add null/undefined guards for optional env vars and optional data fields.
- Keep graceful fallbacks when runtime integrations are unavailable.
- Do not break rendering when analytics or consent services fail to load.
